{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7L3ybJP8yALyyxhsacY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I used the wording we agreed on. The email promises a regular cleaner and a named backup, not the same cleaner every single time.\n\n<final_document>\nSubject: Your own cleaner, and a $99 cleaning to come back\n\nHi,\n\nWhen customers left Brightway last year, the two reasons we heard most were price and a different cleaner showing up too often. You were right about the cleaners, and we've fixed it.\n\nSince July, every customer has their own regular cleaner, plus a named backup for sick days and holidays. You'll always know who's coming to your home. Since we made that change, 1 of our 18 cleaners has left.\n\nAbout price: yes, we cost more than the app services. Our cleaners are employees, not contractors. We pay them $21 an hour, and every visit is insured.\n\nIf you come back, your first cleaning is $99. There's no contract, and you can cancel any time. This offer ends December 31.\n\nJust reply to this email and we'll match you with your regular cleaner.\n\nLisa Grant\nOwner, Brightway Home Cleaning\n</final_document>\n\nA few things to know before you send it:\n\n- **The price after the $99 cleaning isn't in the email** because you didn't know it. Since price was the top reason people left, many readers will want to know before they reply. If you can add a line like \"after that, your regular price is $X,\" the email gets stronger. Even an honest \"$165 every other week for a 3-bedroom\" beats leaving them to guess.\n- **I didn't say the backup is someone they've already met.** You didn't know that. If it is true, add it, because it's the best answer to \"a stranger in my house.\"\n- **\"1 of 18 has left since July\" covers about four months.** That's true and worth saying, but it isn't a full year. I didn't claim that turnover is solved.\n- **I didn't link your pay to cleaners staying.** You paid $21 last year too, when 7 left, so the email presents pay and insurance as what the higher price buys, not as the reason cleaners stay.\n- **Personalisation:** if you can merge in first names, use \"Hi [First name],\" instead of \"Hi,\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":957,"cache_read_input_tokens":10241,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":957},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"cb5af648-1086-46af-969f-2de94eb75425","uuid":"02aca8f6-d083-4941-bc66-e0d27bf46015","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:37:59.161Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7L3ySsGgJBRhXE7MhTt"}
